+## CO-01: proposed Collapsible framework substitutions and bounded lifecycle
+
+Source: pinned [CollapsibleRoot/useCollapsibleRoot](https://github.com/mui/base-ui/blob/47b40521eab921c2756bf9bdb0b0f07fbfdb8c8c/packages/react/src/collapsible/root/useCollapsibleRoot.ts), [CollapsibleTrigger](https://github.com/mui/base-ui/blob/47b40521eab921c2756bf9bdb0b0f07fbfdb8c8c/packages/react/src/collapsible/trigger/CollapsibleTrigger.tsx), [CollapsiblePanel/useCollapsiblePanel](https://github.com/mui/base-ui/blob/47b40521eab921c2756bf9bdb0b0f07fbfdb8c8c/packages/react/src/collapsible/panel/useCollapsiblePanel.ts), useControlled, useTransitionStatus and useAnimationsFinished at immutable Base UI v1.8.0 `47b40521eab921c2756bf9bdb0b0f07fbfdb8c8c`.
+
+The accepted five framework substitutions apply: className to class, render/children to Svelte snippets, refs to bindings/attachments, synthetic to native events and CSS objects to strings. Generated `base-ui-` ID relationships retain the reference registration lifecycle while framework ID bytes differ. Context uses a stable live facade; committed open/callback snapshots preserve the pinned stable callback boundary. A private lifecycle retains idle, starting and deferred ending phases, measures before ending styles, watches cancellation/replacement animations, suppresses initial-open keyframes and handles missing animation APIs/BASE_UI_ANIMATIONS_DISABLED. Temporary CSS uses property-level writes to preserve source sequencing. Framework-specific host cleanup and render/ref timing are bounded substitutions, with observations and limits in the [compatibility record](../parity/collapsible/compatibility.md).
+
+The existing Button helper remains unchanged and contributes inherited D-03 disabled chorded-mousedown focus behavior, with no new parity credit or specific deviation approval. Source-indicated authored alignment !important restoration and replaced-host beforematch issues remain UNVERIFIED until the paired exact-pin browser probes execute; this port does not claim they are verified shared defects or silently correct them. Six external React.Activity cases are unimplemented because state-preserving effect teardown has no bounded CSS-hide/remount equivalent. They earn no credit. No actions or onOpenChangeComplete API is invented.
+
+Rationale: preserve the bounded pinned Collapsible contract using native Svelte lifecycle ownership. Evidence: [component documentation](collapsible.md), [immutable declaration trace and ports](../parity/collapsible/README.md), local DOM/SSR and separate component type/package consumers; secured paired Chromium and final-head gates remain pending at the handoff. Decision status: proposed in [PR #29](https://github.com/sveltery/base/pull/29). The five accepted API substitutions and inherited A-01 initially undefined refs apply; no further behavioral correction approval or complete parity is claimed. This entry does not establish merge eligibility or inflate the shared inventory totals.
